From 7d27f7abe281bbf91a8f74b6bd78020d04d2a647 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 13:17:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] patch 0279 -- log CFG keys silently overridden by a stale env
 var

Diagnosability fix for a trap that has already cost a real-HW iter.

DOSKUTSU.CFG publishes its keys with setenv(name, value, 0), so a DOS `SET`
that is already in the environment wins. That precedence (env > file >
default) is deliberate and stays exactly as it was. What is NOT deliberate
is that it happens in COMPLETE SILENCE: setenv() with overwrite=0 returns 0
(success) even when it changes nothing, so a key whose file value was thrown
away still counts toward the "config: loaded DOSKUTSU.CFG (N keys)" banner.
The count cannot distinguish a key that took effect from one that did not,
and nothing else in the log mentions the loser.

That is exactly how the 2026-07-13 g2k iter (R63B/R63C) burned a cycle: the
CFG said MIDI_SET=orgmid2, a leftover session SET said wiimidi, the engine
dutifully obeyed the environment, logged "MIDI source = 'wiimidi'", and gave
no hint that a config value had been discarded -- so the log read like an
engine bug for a day. realhw's A/B then showed the key-count banner reporting
the SAME number with and without the silent discard, confirming no existing
signal could have caught it.

It is now a USER-facing trap, not just an iter-facing one: SETUP's "Save and
run DOSKUTSU" launches the game in the same DOS session where a stale SET
lives, so the very settings the user just saved can be defeated with no
feedback whatsoever.

The loader (include/doskutsu_config.h, shared with SETUP) now records each
key whose file value lost to a DIFFERENT pre-existing env value; this engine
patch names them:

  config: MIDI_SET=orgmid2 (DOSKUTSU.CFG) OVERRIDDEN by env
          SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_MIDI_SOURCE=wiimidi -- ... Clear the stale
          value with `SET SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_MIDI_SOURCE=` ...

Behavior is untouched: detection only, same setenv calls, same precedence,
same key count. Only new output, and only on divergence.

WARN rather than INFO because a divergence always means someone's intent is
being dropped. Equal values are never recorded, so an iter BAT that
re-asserts a value the CFG already holds stays quiet -- no chatter in the
common case. The line is CONDITIONAL (a clean run emits nothing), so it is
deliberately not a required smoke-gate banner.

Truncation is reported rather than hidden: the loader counts every override
it DETECTS even past the caller's buffer, and the engine says "+N further
... not listed" instead of implying full coverage.

fmt-arg discipline (nx0263): 5 placeholders / 5 args and 2 / 2. Verified with
a DJGPP -fsyntax-only compile of main.cpp against the real sysroot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/main.cpp | 49 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 48 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/main.cpp b/src/main.cpp
index c627dd5e..b18ad19e 100644
--- a/src/main.cpp
+++ b/src/main.cpp
@@ -1503,7 +1503,15 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
   // keys SETUP.EXE manages; setenv overwrite=0 keeps a real DOS `SET`
   // authoritative (env > file > built-in default). No file = no-op =
   // byte-identical to the no-config build. Banner emitted after Logger::init.
-  int _cfg_keys_loaded = doskutsu_cfg_load(NULL);
+  // patch 0279: load via the _ex form so we also learn WHICH keys the file
+  // lost to a pre-existing env var. The precedence itself is unchanged (env
+  // still wins); we only capture the casualties so the banner below can name
+  // them. Logger is not live yet at top-of-main, hence the record-now /
+  // log-later split.
+  dkt_override_t _cfg_ovr[DKT_CFG_OVERRIDE_MAX];
+  int            _cfg_ovr_n     = 0;
+  int            _cfg_keys_loaded =
+      doskutsu_cfg_load_ex(NULL, _cfg_ovr, DKT_CFG_OVERRIDE_MAX, &_cfg_ovr_n);
 
   bool error            = false;
   bool freshstart;
@@ -1571,6 +1579,45 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
     LOG_INFO("config: loaded DOSKUTSU.CFG ({} keys)", _cfg_keys_loaded);
   else
     LOG_INFO("config: no DOSKUTSU.CFG, using built-in defaults");
+
+  // patch 0279: name every CFG key whose value was DISCARDED because a DOS
+  // env var already held a different one. env > file is by design, but it was
+  // SILENT -- setenv(overwrite=0) reports success even when it changes
+  // nothing, so the "(N keys)" count above includes keys that never took
+  // effect. A stale `SET` left in the session therefore defeats the settings
+  // the user just saved in SETUP, invisibly. That is not hypothetical: it cost
+  // a real-HW iter on 2026-07-13 (CFG said MIDI_SET=orgmid2, a leftover
+  // session SET said wiimidi, the engine obeyed the env and said nothing), and
+  // SETUP's "Save and run DOSKUTSU" launches the game in that same session.
+  //
+  // WARN, not INFO: a divergence between the two config sources always means
+  // someone's intent is being dropped on the floor. Agreement is silent (the
+  // loader only records DIFFERING values), so an iter BAT re-asserting a value
+  // the CFG already holds does not chatter.
+  //
+  // CONDITIONAL line -- fires only when a divergence exists. Deliberately NOT
+  // a required smoke-gate banner (a clean run must not emit it).
+  {
+    const int shown =
+        (_cfg_ovr_n < DKT_CFG_OVERRIDE_MAX) ? _cfg_ovr_n : DKT_CFG_OVERRIDE_MAX;
+    for (int i = 0; i < shown; ++i)
+    {
+      LOG_WARN("config: {}={} (DOSKUTSU.CFG) OVERRIDDEN by env {}={} -- the "
+               "environment beats the config file by design (env > file > "
+               "default), so SETUP's value is NOT in effect. Clear the stale "
+               "value with `SET {}=` (empty) and relaunch if you meant the "
+               "saved setting to apply.",
+               _cfg_ovr[i].key, _cfg_ovr[i].file_val, _cfg_ovr[i].env_name,
+               _cfg_ovr[i].env_val, _cfg_ovr[i].env_name);
+    }
+    if (_cfg_ovr_n > shown)
+    {
+      // No silent caps: say what was dropped rather than imply full coverage.
+      LOG_WARN("config: (+{} further env-overridden key(s) detected but not "
+               "listed; buffer holds {})",
+               _cfg_ovr_n - shown, DKT_CFG_OVERRIDE_MAX);
+    }
+  }
 //  SDL_LogSetAllPriority(SDL_LOG_PRIORITY_VERBOSE);
 
   // DOS-PORT (patch 0225, small-polish item 2): register the atexit-chain
-- 
2.47.3

